    {
      "question": "What is the difference between a softbox and an umbrella?",
      "answer": "A softbox produces directional, controlled light with defined edges, ideal for product photography. An umbrella spreads light more broadly and is more forgiving, making it better suited for portraits and quick setups."
    },
    {
      "question": "How long does a product photography project take?",
      "answer": "A standard packshot project of up to 50 products is delivered within 5 business days. Larger catalogs are quoted individually with a detailed schedule."
    },
    {
      "question": "Do you work with clients outside of Lyon?",
      "answer": "Yes. Products can be shipped to our studio from anywhere in Europe, and brand shoots can be organized on location across France."
    }
